# KERO repository environment configuration.
#
# This file is KERO Structured Text (KST). It owns only portable,
# repository-scoped policy. Per-mount refresh overrides are the current schema.
# Keep one active `mount` section per mount; a later section overrides earlier
# sections to preserve comments and manual edits.
#
# Continuous refresh: manual | event (manual is the default)
# mount global
#	refresh event
# mount global
#	refresh manual
#
# Writable synchronization is grant-authorized and is not enabled by a local
# path or filesystem permission alone.
#
# Do not put these settings in this file:
# - KERO_HOME, install paths, PATH entries, or service ports; they are host facts.
# - enrollment, identity, or verification defaults; they belong in
#   KERO_HOME/config.
# - mount source paths or credentials; mounts are explicit terminal requests.
#
# Global preference template: run `kero-host setup` or edit KERO_HOME/config.
# The service stays local-only and writes disposable state only under
# KERO_HOME/.runtime/.
